v 3
d datadictionary: enhanced, over-time-ready codebook generator for multi-wave data
d
d A modern descsave. datadictionary documents the dataset in memory or a set
d of wave files: one codebook row per variable (per variable-wave in
d files mode) with storage type, display format, variable label, value
d label, missingness, distinct values, summary statistics, example
d values, top categories, notes, and characteristics (including the
d srctag char written by combineall/projectbuilder). In files mode it
d detects changes across waves -- variables added or dropped, storage
d types, variable labels, value-label sets, display formats -- which is
d only possible before waves are stitched into one file, because
d stitching destroys per-wave value labels. Results go to the screen, a
d machine-readable .dta, and a multi-sheet Excel workbook.
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260714
d
f datadictionary.ado
f datadictionary.sthlp
